Every opioid-benefit can possibly diminish over a time.
Every opioid-risk can possibly increase over a time.
If a patient continues an opioid-therapy then every clinician should elicit a patient-experience from the patient and should elicit a patient-preference from the patient.
If a patient continues an opioid-therapy then every clinician should periodically review an expected-opioid-benefit with the patient and should periodically review an expected-opioid-risk with the patient.
